  "notes": "Melodic-and-bratty crossover trap that later turned into hard-sample-flip pop-rap. The parameter that carries the ad-libs is `melody.monophonicBias` 0.7 — the research says the vocal is alternately rapped at 16th density and lightly sung, with **heavy ad-lib doubling**, and a note-level doubling probability is the honest way to say that in a MIDI model. `structure` is `call_response` for the same reason. The old-school breakbeat feel of the flip singles shows as `hihat.base` weighted toward 8ths rather than 16ths, which is the opposite of every other half-time entry in this batch. ⚠ `confidence` medium, per the research. The INFERRED parameters are the drum figures and the 808's `slideProb` 0.5 — \"mid-decay 808 with glides on the trap cuts\" and \"light rolls\" are the only descriptions given. ⚠ The 100–115 straight sample-flip lane is present as harmonic material (a major family, `major` in the scale block) rather than as a second tempo: a tempo block cannot state two humps, and this entry keeps the trap hump. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
